{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1160025-question-about-tass","id":1160025,"title":"Question about Tass","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-17T15:25:37-08:00","id":1160025,"title":"Question about Tass","content":"Hi there ! I have a bit of and odd question about Tass, Does it stock up ?<br /> <br /> Let's say my players have a node rating that give them 4 free quintessence per week and 4 in the form of tass per week. If they do not consume the tass, does it replenish itself at the end of the week ? Can they end up with 8 tass ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T16:07:46-08:00","id":1160034,"title":"","content":"I'd probably would rule it not to stock up, but it could depend on what you think the tass is made of. Is it the crystal clear water of a mountain spring, only flowing in moonlit nights? It would flow away and even if you try to block the tass from flowing away, it would get dirty or whatever in some way. Or losing it's &quot;pure-ness&quot; by being held in a non-natural environment.<br /> The fruits of a mystical tree? Become rotten over time.<br /> On the other side, certain Tass could stock up. The destilled special fuel, your etherite character made? Could be stable enough to last for a while.<br /> <br /> Generally, I feel it's too easy to exploit permanent Tass to allow it without some drawback, half-life or risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T21:09:06-08:00","id":1160113,"title":"","content":"Tass has Resonance, so you have to purify it or work with the Resonance. Also, whatever form the Tass is in, it's in some kind of pattern. All patterns decay eventually, so stocking would not be indefinite.<br /> <br /> Also, a big enough pile of Tass stacking up is going to be a beacon for those with Prime or those with senses like Prime such as Garou. They might come collecting if there's a large pile. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T01:17:22-08:00","id":1160147,"title":"","content":"While it's important to observe common sense when it comes to certain kinds of Tass (magic fruit or mushrooms will rot eventually), and there's something to be said of Quintessence leaking from other kinds, it's also important to give your players leeway when it comes to stocking up. Especially if they want to start creating Wonders, which are Tass hogs. It's unreasonable to expect a person to have a pile of 50 Tass to make their Periapt, if that Tass doesn't last the end of the week. Not even getting into Tass that's the right Resonance, which is harder to locate than getting any Tass at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T01:24:16-08:00","id":1160148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1160025-question-about-tass?p=1160147#post1160147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's important to observe common sense when it comes to certain kinds of Tass (magic fruit or mushrooms will rot eventually), and there's something to be said of Quintessence leaking from other kinds, it's also important to give your players leeway when it comes to stocking up. Especially if they want to start creating Wonders, which are Tass hogs. It's unreasonable to expect a person to have a pile of 50 Tass to make their Periapt, if that Tass doesn't last the end of the week. Not even getting into Tass that's the right Resonance, which is harder to locate than getting any Tass at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is right, but as pointed out Tass has Resonance and shines like a beacon, if stocked up. There should be some work put into it to rack up such amounts of Tass savely. Like purifying, transmuting and whatever. This also means, the Resonance will change in some way related to the process, so your mages can actually try to change the Resonances that way AND make it more stable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T02:59:26-08:00","id":1160155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1160025-question-about-tass#post1160025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Let's say my players have a node rating that give them 4 free quintessence per week and 4 in the form of tass per week. If they do not consume the tass, does it replenish itself at the end of the week ? Can they end up with 8 tass ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that it depends on the specifics of the players' True Mages and how they consider Prime, Quintessence and Tass within their Paradigms.<br /> It might also depend on their actions, both recent and from more distant past, in regards to Quintessence and Tass. The interactions between the True Mages who are using the Node could also be considered as part of deciding how to resolve these questions that you are asking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T03:13:41-08:00","id":1160159,"title":"","content":"I do believe Tass, given time will eventually &quot;evaporate&quot; and join the tapestry of creation. How long an individual point of tass should last depends on your ST and the kind of chronicle he or she wants to run. <br /> <br /> Its not really clear what level of prime you need to use tass though... both prime 1 and prime 3 seem to suggest that you can make use of tass at that level. I think it may be that at level 1 you can drain tass and add it to your quintessence/paradox wheel, and at level 3 you can use it directly out of pocket to fuel your spell? I am unclear. <br /> <br /> In any event, it may take some time for your characters to learn enough Prime to use the Tass effectively, and if the ST gives Tass an indefinite shelf life he may be up for a rude awakening when a pc learns how to use it and discovers that the PC's node is a veritable treasure trove of unused tass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T03:31:14-08:00","id":1160161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1160025-question-about-tass?p=1160159#post1160159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do believe Tass, given time will eventually &quot;evaporate&quot; and join the tapestry of creation. How long an individual point of tass should last depends on your ST and the kind of chronicle he or she wants to run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, this. Yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its not really clear what level of prime you need to use tass though... both prime 1 and prime 3 seem to suggest that you can make use of tass at that level. I think it may be that at level 1 you can drain tass and add it to your quintessence/paradox wheel, and at level 3 you can use it directly out of pocket to fuel your spell? I am unclear.<br /> <br /> In any event, it may take some time for your characters to learn enough Prime to use the Tass effectively, and if the ST gives Tass an indefinite shelf life he may be up for a rude awakening when a pc learns how to use it and discovers that the PC's node is a veritable treasure trove of unused tass. </div> </div> </div>Prime 1 is used to fill your Quintessence-wheel beyond your avatar rating, when meditating on Nodes and Junctures. Tass is a more stable, not free flowing form of Quintessence and can be carried around seperatly, as I understand HDYDT. However, it can be absorbed the same way than normal Quintessence, as long as you have it on you. Prime 2 can be used to absorb Tass, that is in your vicinity, but not touching your body (and employ Correspondence 2/Prime 2 for a spell, that basically teleports the Quintessence of the Tass to you, from a far away source).<br /> However, the Core Rulebook seems to rule Prime 3 for this feat, so it may be a mistake in HDYDT.<br /> <br /> All this makes Tass a nice loophole to the whole &quot;Paradox cancels Quintessence&quot;-thing. However, Tass can be stolen physically, even by mundane humans or even animals. (That monkey ate my magic fruit, lol.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T22:58:16-08:00","id":1162367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1160025-question-about-tass?p=1160161#post1160161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All this makes Tass a nice loophole to the whole &quot;Paradox cancels Quintessence&quot;-thing. However, Tass can be stolen physically, even by mundane humans or even animals. (That monkey ate my magic fruit, lol.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Large stores of tass are also a compelling target for other mages or supernatural entities. A large accumulation could weaken the Shroud, or Gauntlet, or Dreamshell or whatever would be appropriate to the resonance of the tass and attract all sorts of unwanted attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":15603,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","user":"PhillyCuriosity","date":".  Added clarification. 11-25-2017, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T21:55:45-08:00","id":1163167,"title":"","content":"Please understand, also, that with high levels of prime you can gain quintessence very easily. Prime 4 lets you destroy objects and gain quintessence, for example. Five lets you get it directly from reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23536-schrodingoethe","name":"Schrodingoethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T03:03:04-08:00","id":1163508,"title":"","content":"If your characters can properly tend to the node, it's all but expected that they can store its tass for a very long time.<br /> <br /> A plenty of tass is best made troublesome via complications rather than deterioration. Bonus points for giving them reason to use it (as if that was ever hard for most characters...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 11-29-2017, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}